K/A","filedAt":"2026-03-11","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000917225","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/917225/000165495426002156/xpl_10ka.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/cf68740cb9e4795ff459c04c7b5efec5794ba4a65972f9f5883a65fee79a5e1f.bin","sha256":"cf68740cb9e4795ff459c04c7b5efec5794ba4a65972f9f5883a65fee79a5e1f"}},{"id":"94775320087e347e8d8dd24aa78723f72da01187d642cfa4a8a2b5bdf8eef074","quote":"Solitario has not applied a discount rate to the recorded asset retirement obligation as the estimated time frame for reclamation is not currently known, as completion reclamation is not expected to occur until the end of the related project life, which would follow future development and operations, the start of which cannot be estimated or assured at this time. Additionally, no depreciation will be recorded on the related asset for the asset retirement obligation until the Lik project goes into operation, which cannot be assured.","context":"Solitario recorded an asset retirement obligation of $125,000 upon the acquisition of the Lik project for Solitario’s estimated reclamation cost of the existing disturbance at the Lik project. This disturbance consists of an exploration camp including certain drill sites and access roads at the camp. The estimate was based upon estimated cash costs for reclamation as determined by Solitario and its joint venture partner Teck and is supported by a permitting bond required by the State of Alaska, for which Solitario has retained a reclamation bond insurance policy in the event Solitario or its 50% partner, Teck, do not complete required reclamation.","section":"Segment reporting","block":180,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001654954-26-002156","form":"10-K/A","filedAt":"2026-03-11","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000917225","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/917225/000165495426002156/xpl_10ka.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw